%I A402456 #12 Nov 22 2026 09:59:55
%S A402456 2,3,7,53,71,83,173,227,241,479,491,1013,2153,5233,18329,33569,80209,
%T A402456 80273,89363,91997,93997
%N A402456 Primes p such that 3*p# + 1 is prime, where prime(n)# = A002110(n).
%C A402456 Primes prime(n) such that A402501(n) is prime.
%C A402456 a(22) > 10^5. - _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
%e A402456 3*2+1 = 7 is prime, so 2 is a term;
%e A402456 3*2*3+1 = 19 is prime, so 3 is a term;
%e A402456 3*2*3*5+1 = 91 = 7*13, so 5 is not a term;
%e A402456 3*2*3*5*7+1 = 631 is prime, so 7 is a term;
%e A402456 3*2*3*5*7*11+1 = 6931 = 29*239, so 11 is not a term;
%e A402456 3*2*3*5*7*11*13+1 = 90091 = 23*3917, so 13 is not a term;
%e A402456 3*2*3*5*7*11*13*17+1 = 1531531 = 43*35617, so 17 is not a term;
%e A402456 3*2*3*5*7*11*13*17*19+1 = 29099071 = 23*1265177, so 19 is not a term.
%o A402456 (PARI) my(P=3); forprime(p=2, 1000, P*=p; if(ispseudoprime(P+1), print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A402456 Cf. A002110 (primorials), A402501.
%Y A402456 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A402456 nonn,more,new
%O A402456 1,1
%A A402456 _Jianing Song_, Nov 19 2026
%E A402456 a(17)-a(21) from _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
